# Payment Integration

- Charge the total stored on the order. Ignore amounts sent by the browser.
- Only `cashier`, `manager`, or `admin` can capture, refund, or void a staff payment. A customer may start payment for their own payable order.
- Persist a provider reference and an idempotency key. A repeated webhook must not capture twice.
- Read the webhook with `express.raw()` on that route only. Verify the signature, then update the payment.
- A success redirect in the browser never marks an order paid. Only a verified webhook or a verified server-side capture does.
- Payment status belongs on the payment document (`pending`, `paid`, `failed`, `refunded`). Refunds restore stock only through the order service.

```javascript
export function paymentWebhook(req, res, next) {
  const valid = verifySignature(req.body, req.get("x-signature"), process.env.PAYMENT_WEBHOOK_SECRET);
  if (!valid) return next(new AppError("Invalid signature", 400));
  next();
}
```

- Do not log card data, raw signatures, or webhook secrets.
